1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Three empires. Thousands of soldiers. And every one of them is marching on a single mountain.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Chera, Chola, Pandya. United, no kingdom could resist them. But this time, the man who stood in their way wore no crown.

3
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Three hundred villages. No fort. No walls. The mountain itself was their defence.

4
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:08,000
His name was Pari. Vel Pari. A man who could never say no to one who asked. And never knew how to bow before power.

5
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:33,000
One day on a forest road, he saw a jasmine vine with nothing to climb. He left his own chariot standing there, and walked home. Who could ever defeat such a man?

6
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Beside him stood Kapilar. He carried no sword — he carried words. The reason we still know Pari today is the songs he sang.

7
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The message of the three kings arrived: submit, and pay tribute — or be destroyed. Pari's answer was the shortest of all: I will not bow.

8
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:39,000
The siege began. Days became weeks. Weeks became months. The forest burned. The rains came. But Parambu did not bow.

9
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:49,500
If an army could not defeat this mountain… what could?

10
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Vel Pari. The full documentary — coming soon.

